      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the number of different starting lineups possible for Coach Grunt's basketball team, we need to calculate the number of ways to choose the remaining 3 players from the 10 available players (since Ace and Zeppo are already in the lineup).\n\nThis problem can be solved using combinations. The number of ways to choose \\( k \\) items from a set of \\( n \\) items is given by the combination formula:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\n\\]\n\nHere, \\( n = 10 \\) (the total number of players minus Ace and Zeppo) and \\( k = 3 \\) (the number of players to be chosen from the remaining 10). Therefore, we need to calculate:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10!}{3!(10-3)!} = \\frac{10!}{3! \\cdot 7!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the \\( 7! \\) in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{3! \\times 7!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{3!}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 3! \\):\n\n\\[\n3! = 3 \\times 2 \\times 1 = 6\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{10}{3} = \\frac{10 \\times 9 \\times 8}{6} = \\frac{720}{6} = 120\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different starting lineups possible is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{120}\n\\]",
